 "captions": [
  {
   "t": "This one useless option makes you spend more money. And you've fallen for it.",
   "s": 0.05,
   "e": 3.51
  },
  {
   "t": "A magazine offered three subscriptions. Online only, fifty-nine dollars. Print only, one hundred twenty-five. Print plus online… also one hundred twenty-five.",
   "s": 3.71,
   "e": 13.67
  },
  {
   "t": "Nobody picks print only. That's the point. It's a decoy.",
   "s": 13.87,
   "e": 17.24
  },
  {
   "t": "When behavioral economist Dan Ariely tested it on MIT students, eighty-four percent chose the expensive combo.",
   "s": 17.44,
   "e": 23.45
  },
  {
   "t": "Remove the decoy… and only thirty-two percent did. Most switched to the cheap option.",
   "s": 23.65,
   "e": 28.18
  },
  {
   "t": "Next time you see a weird middle option, ask yourself: who is that option really for?",
   "s": 28.38,
